---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FAQBlock from '../components/FAQBlock.astro';
import CTABlock from '../components/CTABlock.astro';
import { site, localBusinessSchema } from '../config/site';
const faqs = [
  { question: "Am I a Candidate for Dental Implants?", answer: "If you're missing one or more teeth and in good general health, you're likely a good implant candidate. Dr. Jeziorski will assess your specific situation during your initial consultation." },
  { question: "What Are My Tooth Replacement Options with Dental Implants?", answer: "Options range from single-tooth implants to full mouth restorations and denture stabilization, all tailored to meet your needs." },
  { question: "How Long Do Dental Implants Last?", answer: "With proper care, dental implants can last a lifetime." },
  { question: "Is the Dental Implant Procedure Painful?", answer: "For dental implant treatment, most patients report minimal discomfort, with local anesthesia, or general anesthesia used during the procedure to ensure patient comfort." },
  { question: "What Does the Dental Implant Procedure Involve?", answer: "It typically is oral surgery that will place implants, a healing period, and the attachment of a custom-made crown." },
  { question: "How Much Do Dental Implants Cost?", answer: "Cost varies based on the type and number of implants. Our office offers financing options to make the procedure accessible." },
  { question: "What Are Implants?", answer: "Dental implants represent a groundbreaking leap forward in the realm of dental technology, meticulously crafted to fill the void left by missing teeth with artificial substitutes that not only mirror the appearance of natural teeth but also emulate their feel and functionality to near perfection. These sophisticated devices are securely embedded into the jawbone, serving as robust pillars for the attachment of new teeth. This direct anchorage into the upper jaw bone not only ensures the stability and durability of the implant but also plays a critical role in maintaining the integrity of the jawbone density, and facial structure. By preventing the bone loss commonly associated with missing teeth, dental implants contribute significantly to preserving the natural contour of the face and overall oral health. Their design and implementation are the culmination of years of scientific research and clinical advancements, making them a preferred choice for individuals looking to restore their smiles to their natural glory." },
  { question: "Are Implants Safe?", answer: "Absolutely. Dental implants have a high success rate and are considered a safe and effective solution for patients replacing missing teeth. With proper care and maintenance, risks and complications of implant failure are minimal." },
  { question: "Are Implants Worth it?", answer: "Considering their natural appearance, ability to improve quality of life, and long-term benefits, dental implants are an incredibly beneficial option and worthwhile investment for many patients seeking to replace missing teeth." },
  { question: "What is All-on-4?", answer: "All-on-4 treatment utilizes the integrity of four strategically-placed dental implants to support a hybrid, full-arch restoration. This streamlined device merges the efficiency of dentures with the comfort and functionality of dental implants. Only in this case, there are no bulky \"plates\" across the roof of your mouth or devices to take out at night; everything is naturally designed and permanently affixed into place.\n\nWith All-on-4 implants, a \"U\" shaped appliance is permanently attached to the four implants underneath. All of the teeth in your upper or lower arch are replaced at the same time." },
  { question: "What Are the Benefits of All-On-4 Dental Implants?", answer: "Compared to popular tooth replacement options like dentures or partials, Phoenix All-on-4 treatment offers: Improved speech patterns, Long-term functionality of dental implants, Better comfort and stability, No dietary restrictions, Enhanced bone health.\n\nOnce placed, dental implants integrate with your bone and become a permanent part of your new smile. Their ability to support your facial tissues helps you maintain natural fullness in your lips, cheeks, and overall profile (essentially preventing premature aging caused by tooth loss.)\n\nToday's dental implants have the highest success rate of any restorative treatment in modern dentistry. Their integrity allows our Phoenix dentists to use as few as 4-6 implants total to support a full-arch restoration spanning from one side of your mouth to the other. Although All-on-4 is not a dental bridge, it is similar to bridges in the way they only follow the contour of your bite, rather than rest in the roof of your mouth. Additionally, implants are stronger than anatomical teeth, meaning you can enjoy various textures of foods without having to worry whether each bite is soft or small enough to chew.\n\nPlus, dental implants are designed to last an entire lifetime. Once they're placed, it's possible to care for and maintain implants for decades to come.\n\nLiving with All-on-4 dental implants means you can go about your daily activities almost as if you had natural teeth all over again. You won't have to think twice. Not to mention you can completely avoid the embarrassment of a denture accidentally slipping when you speak, or having to take it out each night." },
  { question: "What Should I Expect During the All-On-4 Procedure?", answer: "Getting All-on-4 implants always starts with a consultation to determine if you qualify for this innovative procedure. From there, we'll plan an exam and detailed treatment planning process that outlines the steps and costs involved. Once it's time to have your implants placed, we'll fit you with an interim prosthesis as your implants integrate, then install a permanent new restoration once everything has fully healed. The actual placement is more comfortable than you might expect!" },
  { question: "How Much Do All-On-4 Dental Implants Cost?", answer: "The cost of All-on-4 dental implants will slightly vary from one person to the next. Why? Because other factors such as the need for bone grafting, gum augmentation, extractions, or even sedation will all play a role in the total cost of your treatment. Even the level of restoration you select (based on the materials used) will impact the total implant cost. On top of that, whether or not you have dental insurance also comes into play.\n\nTo ensure full disclosure of your dental implant costs, our treatment coordinators will compile your care plan—including details such as insurance coverage and specific steps necessary—then present a printed plan that outlines the entire process. Even the number of visits will be discussed. At this time, you'll know the total estimated price of your All-on-4 implants. We can also discuss financing options if you would like to break the process up into modest monthly payments. You'll have all of the information you need before committing to treatment." },
  { question: "What are Clear Aligners?", answer: "Clear Aligners are an \"invisible\" type of braces that uses a series of aligners—instead of brackets and wires—to move your teeth. You wear each pair for about two weeks before progressing to the next set. Pair by pair, your aligners gently nudge your teeth into alignment.\n\nDeveloped over 20 years ago, Clear Aligners provide proven, predictable, and efficient results for people with mild to severe crowding and gaps." },
  { question: "Are Clear Aligners Better Than Braces?", answer: "Most of our Phoenix Clear Aligner patients prefer them over traditional braces because of advantages like: Freedom to enjoy any food (no dietary restrictions!), Easier home care and maintenance, Gentler and more comfortable design, Transparent, for ultimate discreteness, Removable for flossing, eating, etc., Digitally mapped in advance.\n\nThe convenience and discrete nature of clear aligners make them a popular choice for adult orthodontic therapy. Teens make great candidates, too! Progression of teeth movement occurs by changing out aligners, you won't have to schedule \"adjustment\" appointments. Enjoy fewer and shorter trips to our office throughout your clear aligner experience." },
  { question: "Clear Aligners Cost", answer: "One of the most common questions people have is, \"How much do Clear Aligners cost?\" There are several varying factors that can influence the total price of Clear Aligners in Phoenix. Here are just a few:\n\nThe Length of Treatment: Since clear aligners use sets of trays to systematically move your teeth, requiring fewer or greater pairs of aligners can ultimately influence the overall price of treatment.\n\nUnderlying Dental Concerns: Clear aligners are only meant for people with healthy teeth and gums. You may need other services leading up to clear aligners to correct decay/cavities, gum disease, or other factors at hand.\n\nYour Insurance Benefits Coverage: Some dental benefit plans cover the cost of braces or clear aligners up to a predetermined amount. How much is covered will depend on your unique policy and set benefits. Be sure to bring a copy of your insurance benefit card with you to your appointment.\n\nRest assured that regardless of your benefits coverage, we offer affordable payment options for every budget. Easily enjoy low or no-interest financing on all clear aligner treatments, allowing you to tap into flexible monthly amounts that fit your lifestyle.\n\nFor a specific price quote for clear aligners, be sure to schedule a one-on-one evaluation." },
  { question: "Alternatives to Clear Aligners", answer: "The most common alternatives to clear aligners are traditional braces, ClearCorrect, and many more. Depending on how your teeth fit together and the budget you're working with, some teeth alignment systems may be better for your situation.\n\nDuring your evaluation, we'll discuss the advantages or disadvantages that you'll want to consider, based on your needs. From there you'll be able to make an educated decision about selecting the best braces (even if it's an alternative to clear aligners) for you and your family." },
  { question: "What is the Process for Getting Clear Aligners?", answer: "Thanks to unique planning software, Clear Aligners allows you to virtually preview your results before the treatment is scheduled to start.\n\nDuring your exam, our Phoenix clear aligner dentist will evaluate your bite, your oral health status and scan your teeth, take photos and submit these records to determine approximately how many sets of trays will be needed to align your smile. Each set of aligners is worn for two-week intervals. Since clear aligners are digitally planned, we will be able to create a workup that shows what type of results you can expect and to determine approximately how long it will take to achieve your goal. You'll have a good idea of what to expect before committing to anything.\n\nOnce you approve and pay for your case, the aligners are printed and shipped to our practice. There's no need to visit an off-site orthodontist's office." },
  { question: "How Long do I Need to Wear Clear Aligner Correctors for?", answer: "Wearing your clear aligner trays as directed will help you reduce the overall time requirement of your orthodontic treatment. Our patients with minor tooth misalignment who are straightening their smiles for minor aesthetic reasons may be able to complete clear aligners in just 4-6 months. However, most traditional bite alignment is completed in about 12-24 months." },
  { question: "What is ClearCorrect?", answer: "ClearCorrect is a digitally mapped aligner system that uses 3D scanning technology to plan your tooth movement and guide them into a straighter position. It uses systematic pairs of alignment trays that you change out as directed, to gradually (and safely) align your bite.\n\nEvery set of ClearCorrect trays is made from transparent, BPA-free plastic material that's smooth and customized to your unique smile." },
  { question: "Is ClearCorrect Better Than Braces?", answer: "If given the choice, most of our Phoenix orthodontic patients tell us that ClearCorrect is far better than braces. Simply because it allows for added perks and conveniences, like: Fewer and shorter trips to the dentist's office, Transparent aligners no one can see, Freedom to eat all of your favorite foods, Zero modification to your daily brushing and flossing routine, Discreet for social and professional interactions, Improved comfort, Digital design." },
  { question: "ClearCorrect Cost", answer: "The price for ClearCorrect in Phoenix can vary, depending on a few different factors. To provide you with a precise quote, we will need to evaluate your bite, have our care coordinators incorporate your insurance benefit details (if applicable), and review other factors that could influence your treatment. Fortunately, after your initial exam, you'll have a good idea as to the length and cost of ClearCorrect for your given situation.\n\nThe Type of Insurance Benefits Coverage You Have: Depending on the type of dental benefits plan you carry; your benefits may include orthodontic coverage in some situations. Our treatment coordinators will communicate with your carrier to get an itemized breakdown of what's included. Please note that if you don't have insurance coverage on braces, we offer flexible payment plan options for every budget.\n\nHow Long Your Treatment Will Take: The length of time required to correct your bite influences how many pairs of aligners you'll need. And the number of aligners required can significantly impact the total cost of ClearCorrect. Some people need far fewer, while others need more.\n\nExisting Gum or Dental Problems: Active decay/cavities or gum disease must be addressed before initiating any type of orthodontic treatment. However, ClearCorrect can be used alongside gum therapy to help reduce your risk of recurring infection!\n\nContact our office to reserve an exam to receive a precise breakdown of which fees may be involved." },
  { question: "Alternatives to ClearCorrect Aligners", answer: "Some of the most popular alternatives to ClearCorrect aligners include traditional braces, clear aligners, and many others. Each system has its advantages, but people who prefer invisible aligners and affordability tend to lean toward ClearCorrect. ClearCorrect is backed by over 15 years of success, providing comfortable—and predictable—teeth straightening for adults and teens throughout the world." },
  { question: "What is the Process for Getting ClearCorrect?", answer: "First, you'll want to visit our Phoenix ClearCorrect provider to find out if you qualify for invisible braces. We'll screen for oral infections and assess the way your teeth bite together. Typically, a series of photographs, digital scans, impressions, or X-rays are taken. At that point, we can estimate the length of your ClearCorrect treatment and work up an itemized care plan that breaks down all of the steps, fees, benefits, etc.\n\nIf you decide you're ready to get ClearCorrect, we order your aligners and have them shipped to our office. You'll take several pairs of trays home in advance, changing them out as directed. About every other month, you'll stop by our Phoenix dentist's office for a brief check-in to ensure everything is moving along as it ought to." },
  { question: "How Long Do I Need to Wear ClearCorrect Aligners for?", answer: "ClearCorrect aligners need to be worn for a minimum of 22 hours per day and changed out as directed (usually every two weeks.) Wearing your aligners as prescribed helps to ensure a predictable treatment outcome. Only remove your teeth-straightening trays for meals, brushing, flossing, or if you're drinking anything other than water." },
  { question: "Are Dental Implants Safe?", answer: "Dental implants are a safe and effective solution for replacing missing teeth. At our practice, we adhere to stringent sterilization and safety protocols to ensure the highest standards of care. Our dentists have extensive training and experience in implantology, providing treatments that meet the individual needs of each patient." },
  { question: "Are Dental Implants Worth It?", answer: "For many patients, the benefits of dental implants far outweigh the costs. Single-tooth implants are a long-term investment in your oral health, functionality, and self-esteem. They offer a permanent solution that can prevent further dental issues and provide a cost-effective alternative to bridges and dentures, which may need to be replaced over time." },
  { question: "How long do implants last?", answer: "With proper care, implants can last a lifetime. Keeping up with your oral hygiene can prevent issues with the implant and extend the life of your crown. A crown may last for a decade or more, depending on use and care." },
  { question: "Is the procedure painful?", answer: "Discomfort is minimal, and we use effective anesthesia and sedation options. We'll provide aftercare instructions that will guide you in managing your pain after the procedure." },
  { question: "How do I care for my implant?", answer: "Care for it just like your natural teeth, with regular brushing and flossing." },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`FAQ — ${site.name}`}
  description={`Common questions about dental services at ${site.name}. Insurance, appointments, treatments, and more.`}
  schema={localBusinessSchema}
>
  <section class="bg-surface-2">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="section-heading mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-neutral-mid">
          Quick answers to the questions we hear most often. Can't find what you're looking for? Call us at <a href={`tel:${site.phone.replace(/\D/g, '')}`} class="text-brand-primary font-semibold">{site.phone}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <FAQBlock faqs={faqs} heading="" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <CTABlock phone={site.phone} />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
